   },
   {
    "frase": "## 2.6.",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2.6"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Solubility is a thermodynamic property of solids with significant consequences for the pharmaceutical industry [52], particularly with regard to the oral bioavailability of APIs.",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "52"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "There are several techniques that are currently used to address this issue [53,54,55,56], including the formation of multicomponent materials, such as cocrystals and salts [57].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "53,54",
     "57"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "The solubility obtained for CIP at pH 6.8 was consistent with other values reported under the same conditions, thus confirming the validity of the method (Figures S12 and S13, Table S3) [19].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "19"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Such behavior has been reported previously [19,69].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "19,69"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
